"Trace DisplayLockDocumentState in ScopedForceActivatableDisplayLocks"
(crbug 576723181, restricted; no CVE listed yet): a use-after-free.
AIPageContentAgent's ContentBuilder::Build() kept untraced raw
DisplayLockDocumentState pointers on the heap, so a child frame detached
and garbage-collected during UpdateLifecycle() left them dangling.
chromium/src main commit 64154b3895e788731c0095472df4881df78c38be
(main@{#1729512}), merged on 2026-10-30 to 158 and to 157 as
64f70faa4080d01505cc88259d6361c7e87a67cc (refs/branch-heads/8103@{#989},
after the 157.0.8103.33 tag). This is the 157 merge, without its test.
Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

